[[0,1334646,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T01:08:17","SUPA_FUPA","",[],"<p>I like eating yogurts as snacks and light meals because they're refreshing and helps cleans your system out and makes you feel good. I've also been collecting coupons for yogurt because yogurt is already cheap and healthy so might have another coupon for this. I had so much coupons that when I heard a fat talking about how its hungry, I handed it the coupon and it glared at me.</p>\n<p><strong>SUPA_FUPA:</strong> I have so much of these coupons and they expire at the end of the month soon. Here's a coupon for you since you said you're hungry.</p>\n<p><strong>Obeast:</strong> I'm sorry but I don't like yogurt and that's bird food. I want pizza!</p>\n<p><strong>SUPA_FUPA:</strong> I like pizza from these restaurants since they're closer to the actual Italian pizzas plus they're much tastier too!</p>\n<p><strong>Obeast:</strong> They're so expensive! I like Pizza Hut!</p>\n<p><strong>SUPA_FUPA:</strong> I don't like it. If I wanted to have my guilty pleasures, I'd chose the one with the highest qualities. Other than that, I'm sticking with fruits, yogurt, and smoked salmon. I like to buy rye bread and make smørrebrød. Toasted rye, cream cheese, capers, and smoked salmon is tasty and I'm having that for dinner tonight.</p>\n<p><strong>Obeast:</strong> That's not going to fill me up and that sounds like rabbit food. Yogurt is slimy and icky! I gotta eat and enjoy it! Yogurt is expensive and I'd rather have fries over a cup of yogurt because they taste better.</p>\n<p><strong>SUPA_FUPA:</strong> Geez I'm just trying to help you out.</p>\n<p>And I walked away wishing this was a joke but its not. I mean come on! Yogurt is cheap and filling! They make great snacks too! Then again, we're talking about obeasts who have messed up perceptions on food portions compared to humans.</p>\n<p>Yogurt has protein, sometimes actual fruit, and its really healthy! Unless one is lactose intolerant, I don't see why anyone should not eat yogurt. Apparently, &quot;french fries&quot; are real food than yogurt according to obeasts which baffles me.</p>","Triggered a fat by giving it a coupon for yogurt.","","fatpeoplehate"],[1,6518327,0,2,1,1,"2016-10-09T01:21:49","ButterSnuffer","",[],"<p>SUPA! - long time fan :)</p>\n<p>Are you subtly shitlording from the beginning here?</p>\n<p>Part of me thinks you're not, and you actually impart this good advice to buttersnuffers in good faith.</p>\n<p>Most of me hopes you're just a fucking savage tho :D</p>\n<p>Love the narratives and screenplay writing style too</p>"],[2,6518431,6518327,2,0,2,"2016-10-09T01:41:30","SUPA_FUPA","[e]",[],"<p>Yup! Doing more shitlording since I just quit my job! Just got out of a few job interviews and there were fats there too and I'm puzzled how they can do their jobs. Even more shocking is that one of these interviews was a fucking EMT company and there were some fats in the dispatching office. The biggest irony there is that they handed me a questionnaire that asked me how often do I take care of my physical health and how cautious am I watching what I eat before the interview. Sadly, despite being qualified for the job and taking care of myself, I was not offered the dispatcher position in the EMT company and was told to call back later. I don't understand how an EMT company with shitlordy questions hire fats.</p>\n<p>I do the screenplay writing style because the conversation is funny plus easier to explain the contents of our conversations.</p>"],[3,6518499,6518431,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T01:53:21","Runway22L","",[],"<p>That with the salmon sounds really good! Yogurt is food for the gods!</p>"],[4,6518508,6518499,0,0,0,"2016-10-09T01:55:38","SUPA_FUPA","",[],"<p>Yogurt is also cheaper than most processed snacks! I don't understand why fats hate on yogurt so much. I'm pretty sure food stamp covers yogurt too but no fats on disability use their food stamp on junk food instead! There's always awesome deals on yogurt too of all brands so I don't see the excuse of not eating healthy.</p>"],[5,6518924,6518508,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T03:10:59","ScootyPoofTipper","",[],"<p>They hate it because it's not ice cream.</p>"],[3,6518545,6518431,1,1,0,"2016-10-09T02:01:53","ButterSnuffer","",[],"<p>Dammit! call them back - chase the job! I can't fucking wait for the stories... :D</p>\n<p>Go for it SUPA, we need you back 'gainfully' employed :)</p>"],[4,6518555,6518545,0,0,0,"2016-10-09T02:03:47","SUPA_FUPA","",[],"<p>Will do! I have upcoming job interviews and my job will have to be part-time so I can focus more on my schooling. I just hope I don't deal with any sassy fats in the workplace.</p>"],[5,6518614,6518555,1,1,0,"2016-10-09T02:15:27","ButterSnuffer","",[],"<p>I really hope you do.. you toasted rye and caper eating mofo ;)</p>"],[1,6518384,0,24,0,24,"2016-10-09T01:34:14","Carsandsarcasm","",[],"<p>&quot;I want as much quantity of the lowest possible quality as possible.&quot;</p>"],[2,6519273,6518384,8,0,8,"2016-10-09T04:15:11","Plavonica","[e]",[],"<p>Bingo. It's surprising how often a group motorbike ride ends in beetus. Cheap beetus. Hence why I usually ride alone. I would rather explore the roads by myself and starve than eat that crap. Then again, regular grocery stores are everywhere so there really is no excuse for you fat Harley riders.</p>\n<p>And yes, I <em>can</em> get away with 400cc less because I don't weigh as much as my motorcycle. </p>"],[1,6518779,0,14,0,14,"2016-10-09T02:44:57","Trotrot","[e]",[],"<p>&quot;rabbit food&quot;</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>yogurt</p>\n<p>cream cheese</p>\n<p>salmon</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This butter-chugger wouldn't know what &quot;rabbit food&quot; was if it smacked its greasy, puffed up face into some. Then again, anything not laced with over 50% of a normal human's daily intake of sodium, sugar, and fat tastes like cardboard to these cows, they've desensitized their palates by eating garbage their whole lives.</p>"],[2,6520741,6518779,4,0,4,"2016-10-09T11:59:38","Vonjaderyn","[e]",[],"<p>They also act as though their palate is a fixed thing that cannot ever change. it's not. If you want to eat less salt, your palate acclimates to the sodium-free food within a few weeks. But they can't even go a day without changing their diet back (genuhtics of course), so I don't what I'm expecting...</p>"],[1,6518872,0,6,0,6,"2016-10-09T03:01:48","veganesthie","",[],"<p>Yogurt is rabbit food now?!?! </p>"],[1,6519086,0,4,0,4,"2016-10-09T03:38:16","Cerryo","",[],"<p>Man I get whole milk Greek yogurt sometimes... just milk and bacteria. It is so fatty. Thus fat people should like it.</p>\n<p>But I think they probably don't eat such things very often? I imagine them buying fat-free high-sugar varieties instead. :(</p>"],[2,6519214,6519086,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T03:57:03","SUPA_FUPA","",[],"<p>I eat Icelandic style yogurt; Siggi's is a good brand. More savory than sweet.</p>"],[3,6519247,6519214,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T04:06:30","Cerryo","",[],"<p>I am not familiar with Icelandic yogurt. Siggi's website says it is sold in my area, so I will try it if I remember. It does look good.</p>"],[4,6519267,6519247,0,0,0,"2016-10-09T04:12:00","SUPA_FUPA","",[],"<p>Oh you'll love it! Very savory and thicker than the average yogurt.</p>"],[3,6519838,6519214,2,0,2,"2016-10-09T06:24:46","SmallElfinBody","",[],"<p>You mean skyr?</p>"],[4,6521626,6519838,0,0,0,"2016-10-09T15:04:06","SUPA_FUPA","",[],"<p>Yes</p>"],[1,6519133,0,9,0,9,"2016-10-09T03:43:55","Hamdragonslayer","",[],"<p>&quot;I'll have 2000 of your cheapest calories please&quot;</p>"],[1,6519237,0,9,0,9,"2016-10-09T04:03:38","waterteacoffeelee","",[],"<p>Most lactose intolerants can have Greek yogurt! Greek yogurt has a lot of the lactose strained out so it's fine unless you're allergic to dairy. </p>"],[2,6519643,6519237,2,0,2,"2016-10-09T05:40:14","Shoeshopper21","[e]",[],"<p>Most lactose intolerants can have regular yogurt too since bacteria in it breaks down most of lactose! Well tbh, lactose intolerant people can have any lactose they want but the consequences are the reason we generally avoid it (explosive diarrhea, severe stomach cramps, and tons of gas). Reason being that since our bodies don't produce enough lactase enzyme, most of the lactose ends up going to our intestines, where bacteria have a party breaking down lactose (byproducts of which irritates our intestines and the other byproduct is gas) but since yogurt contains lots of &quot;good&quot; bacteria, most lactose is already broken down. I can only eat yogurt without experiencing any lactose intolerance symptoms.</p>"],[2,6519720,6519237,2,0,2,"2016-10-09T05:58:27","HelloPanda26","",[],"<p>Lactose intolerant here! The second shelf of my fridge is specifically reserved for Greek yogurts! So tasty!!</p>"],[2,6520601,6519237,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T11:16:32","wmeth","",[],"<p>There you go, thinking that fats know things ahhahaha</p>"],[1,6519484,0,5,0,5,"2016-10-09T05:03:08","DevilsMonkey","",[],"<p>If you're not finding yogurt filling enough mix a bit of granola in there. That shit is good and still relatively healthy.</p>"],[1,6519640,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-09T05:39:56","theepilepticferret","",[],"<p>Man, I was salivating just reading your post. Smoked salmon + capers + cream cheese on some sort of bread is the bomb. If I make it, I usually toss it on a bagel, but next time I'll try rye.</p>\n<p>I'm lactose intolerant too, although not severely as I can still have some dairy, yogurt included. The bacteria in the yogurt helps break down the lactose sugars so I can actually eat it without getting a stomache ache. I love having Greek yogurt after a workout, or for breakfast.</p>"],[1,6520209,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T09:05:20","bunnee","",[],"<p>Yay for Nordic shitlords! o/</p>"],[2,6521637,6520209,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T15:05:47","SUPA_FUPA","",[],"<p>I'm not Nordic but I love them and know people from there. I'm Asian but I find Nordic culture fascinating. =P</p>"],[3,6539149,6521637,0,0,0,"2016-10-11T18:56:14","bunnee","",[],"<p>Woo, greetings from up here! Feel free to hit me with a private message if you wanna chat about Nordic culture. :)</p>"],[1,6520734,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T11:56:57","Vonjaderyn","",[],"<p>As a vegan, I get the rabbit food comments <em>all the time</em> from fats. I feel you, OP.</p>\n<p>Maybe if hams focuses on eating filling, healthy food rather than shoveling oily and sugary shit food into their <s>garbage chutes</s> mouths, they would stop bitching so much.</p>"],[1,6521105,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T13:36:21","Visitresss","",[],"<p>For the lactose intolerant, I'm sure there is an option. The bacteria in kefir normally eat all the lactose before humans taste it.</p>"],[1,6521198,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-09T13:50:54","l23r","",[],"<p>I am lactose intolerant and wish I could eat yogurt after reading this post! Unfortunately the grocery store that sells the lactose free kind is closed today.</p>"],[1,6522226,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-09T16:27:55","shezbot","",[],"<p>I probably have close to 20 Greek yogurts on the top shelf in my fridge right now. When they go on sale 10/$10, I stock up. I usually eat one a day for lunch so at $1 each, that's a bargain. AND SO GOOD. </p>"]]
